        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jay-Z, Thurston Moore\n- Albums: Reasonable Doubt, The Blueprint, The Black Album, Ununiform\n- Organizations: Rolling Stone, Roc-A-Fella Records, Priority Records\n- Topics: rankings, album releases, engineering credits\n\nFacts:\n- Reasonable Doubt was released on June 25, 1996, by Roc-A-Fella Records and Priority Records.\n- Rolling Stone ranked Jay-Z's albums Reasonable Doubt (1996), The Blueprint (2001), and The Black Album (2003) among The 500 Greatest Albums of All Time.\n- In Rolling Stone's 2004 edition of the 100 Greatest Guitarists of All Time, Thurston Moore was ranked 34th.\n- Jay-Z co-engineered the album Ununiform.",
